00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:46.440
which will also publish and
schedule to run on Posit

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:50.160
Connect. We'll also apply a
custom theme to this second

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:52.200
quarto document to make
it look really nice.

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:57.960
Now for our data, we are
going to use Posit's public package

00:06:57.960 --> 00:07:00.060
manager here. So I
click on this link.

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:09.960
So this is a free hosted
service that provides standard

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:13.920
mirrors of popular r
and Python repositories,

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:15.120
including cran,

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:17.160
bioconductor, and PyPI.

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:21.660
Additionally, you can track
repository changes over time.

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:24.540
You can freeze repositories
to specific dates,

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:28.920
and install packages as pre
compiled Linux binaries.

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:33.120
Now this instance of package
manager is used by hundreds of

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:36.480
data science teams throughout the
world and will serve as a

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:39.660
good proxy for understanding
our package download trends.

